WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.240
Hi, I'm Sandra, from HEARa. 

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.080
Welcome to Day 9 of our 
10-day Lip reading Challenge, 

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.639
designed to help you develop
and practice your lip reading skills! 

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.940
Hearing loss can have a 
profound impact on your life. 

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.749
It touches every interaction.

6
00:00:17.749 --> 00:00:19.337
It can affect your career,

7
00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:20.529
your relationships,

8
00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:21.720
and your happiness.

9
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.940
Join me to explore tips and tricks
on this YouTube channel 

10
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:32.580
to bring confidence and clarity
to relationships in all areas of your life. 

11
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.800
We're back to three mangoes with one stone
for Day 9. 

12
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.940
We have three sounds
in our homophone group today. 

13
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:51.239
The sounds are SH, CH, and J.
These sounds look alike 

14
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.069
on the lips.

15
00:00:52.069 --> 00:00:53.451
To make these sounds,

16
00:00:53.451 --> 00:00:58.320
your lips are thrust forward,
almost like a square shape.

17
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.940
Not only that though,
there's something happening with your tongue. 

18
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:11.400
Try it.
Say the words SHOP, CHOP, and JUDGE. 

19
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.799
You may have noticed
that the blade of your tongue, 

20
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.600
which is just behind the tip,
is touching the roof of your mouth 

21
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:30.960
when you make these sounds.
Try it again: CHOP, SHOP, JUDGE. 

22
00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.060
There's another three for one
in today's practice. 

23
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.540
You're going to be working on substitution, 

24
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.159
a little bit of memory work,
and lip reading skills. 

25
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.720
I'm also going to amp up
the difficulty a little bit. 

26
00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.520
I think you're ready for it.

27
00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.706
I'm going to start with substitution practice.

28
00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:04.620
So I'll say sentences with SH, CH, or J
errors and you will have to substitute 

29
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.260
the appropriate sound
to get the right answer. 

30
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.760
So if it's an SH error,
then you need to substitute 

31
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:17.340
a CH or a J to get the right answer.
I'm also going to put some 

32
00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.360
P, B, and M and F and V errors
in there too.

33
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.540
Are you ready?
As always, the answers are written below. 

